<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady in holiday trade.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady in holiday trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices for plant delivery rose 50 rupees, but trading was quiet in central India as markets were closed for a religious holiday.</p>
<p>Soymeal and soyoil prices were increased slightly today.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand while soyoil solvent was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was up by $5 per tonne and quoted at $250-252 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was steady and quoted at $92-93 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 3,200-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
